@startuml 04-class-design-patterns
'============================================================================
'  Sunrise Dental Clinic - CLASS DIAGRAM: the design patterns
'  CIS6003 Advanced Programming (WRIT1), Task A and Task B
'
'  Six patterns are used in this system. Two of them are shown on other
'  diagrams because that is where they belong: Builder on diagram 02, with the
'  Appointment it builds, and Repository and MVC on diagram 03, with the tiers.
'
'  The four shown here are the ones that work together and are hard to see in
'  the code one file at a time: the Factory that chooses a pricing rule, the
'  Strategy that is that rule, the Template Method that stops the three rules
'  drifting apart, and the Observer that announces a booking.
'============================================================================

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor #F0FDFA
    BorderColor #0F766E
    HeaderBackgroundColor #CCFBF1
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
    BorderColor #B45309
}

title Sunrise Dental Clinic - Design patterns in the business tier

'============================================================================
'  FACTORY + STRATEGY + TEMPLATE METHOD: how a bill is priced
'============================================================================

class BillingService {
    - billingStrategyFactory : BillingStrategyFactory
    --
    + generateBill(appointmentNo : String, manualDiscount : BigDecimal, issuedBy : User) : Bill
}

class BillingStrategyFactory <<(P,#B45309) Factory>> {
    - {static} SURGICAL_TREATMENTS : Set<String>
    - {static} CONSULTATION_TREATMENTS : Set<String>
    --
    + strategyFor(treatment : Treatment) : BillingStrategy
}

interface BillingStrategy <<(P,#B45309) Strategy>> {
    + getName() : String
    + calculate(context : BillingContext) : BillCharge
}

abstract class AbstractBillingStrategy <<(P,#B45309) Template Method>> {
    # {static} LOYALTY_VISIT_THRESHOLD : int = 5
    # {static} LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : BigDecimal = 0.10
    --
    + {final} calculate(context : BillingContext) : BillCharge
    # {abstract} treatmentCostFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # {abstract} consultationFeeFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # {abstract} baseExplanation(context : BillingContext) : String
    # loyaltyDiscountFor(context : BillingContext, treatmentCost : BigDecimal) : BigDecimal
    # explanationFor(context : BillingContext, discount : BigDecimal) : String
}

class StandardBillingStrategy {
    + getName() : String
    # treatmentCostFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # consultationFeeFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # baseExplanation(context : BillingContext) : String
}

class SurgicalBillingStrategy {
    - {static} STERILISATION_RATE : BigDecimal = 0.15
    --
    + getName() : String
    # treatmentCostFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # consultationFeeFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # baseExplanation(context : BillingContext) : String
}

class ConsultationOnlyBillingStrategy {
    + getName() : String
    # treatmentCostFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # consultationFeeFor(context : BillingContext) : BigDecimal
    # baseExplanation(context : BillingContext) : String
}

class BillingContext {
    - treatment : Treatment
    - consultationFee : BigDecimal
    - completedVisitCount : int
    --
    + getTreatment() : Treatment
    + getConsultationFee() : BigDecimal
    + getCompletedVisitCount() : int
}

class BillCharge {
    - treatmentCost : BigDecimal
    - consultationFee : BigDecimal
    - discount : BigDecimal
    - strategyName : String
    - explanation : String
    --
    + getTotal() : BigDecimal
    - {static} money(amount : BigDecimal) : BigDecimal
}

'============================================================================
'  OBSERVER: how a booking is announced
'============================================================================

class AppointmentService <<(S,#0F766E) Subject>> {
    - observers : List<AppointmentObserver>
    --
    + register(request : BookingRequest, createdBy : User) : Appointment
    - announce(event : Consumer<AppointmentObserver>) : void
}

interface AppointmentObserver <<(P,#B45309) Observer>> {
    + onAppointmentBooked(appointment : Appointment) : void
    + onAppointmentCancelled(appointment : Appointment) : void
    + onAppointmentRescheduled(appointment : Appointment) : void
}

class EmailAppointmentObserver {
    - enabled : boolean
    + onAppointmentBooked(appointment : Appointment) : void
    + onAppointmentCancelled(appointment : Appointment) : void
}

class LoggingAppointmentObserver {
    + onAppointmentBooked(appointment : Appointment) : void
    + onAppointmentCancelled(appointment : Appointment) : void
    + onAppointmentRescheduled(appointment : Appointment) : void
}

'============================================================================
'  SINGLETON: the clinic's settings
'============================================================================

class ClinicConfiguration <<(P,#B45309) Singleton>> {
    - clinicName : String
    - consultationFee : BigDecimal
    - openingTime : LocalTime
    - closingTime : LocalTime
    - appointmentSlotMinutes : int
    --
    + load() : void
    + reload() : void
    + isWithinOpeningHours(time : LocalTime) : boolean
    + isOnSlotBoundary(time : LocalTime) : boolean
}

'============================================================================
'  RELATIONSHIPS
'============================================================================

BillingService --> BillingStrategyFactory : asks which rule
BillingStrategyFactory ..> BillingStrategy : <<creates>>
BillingService ..> BillingContext : builds
BillingService ..> BillCharge : receives

AbstractBillingStrategy ..|> BillingStrategy
StandardBillingStrategy --|> AbstractBillingStrategy
SurgicalBillingStrategy --|> AbstractBillingStrategy
ConsultationOnlyBillingStrategy --|> AbstractBillingStrategy

BillingStrategy ..> BillingContext : reads
BillingStrategy ..> BillCharge : produces

AppointmentService "1" o--> "0..*" AppointmentObserver : announces to
EmailAppointmentObserver ..|> AppointmentObserver
LoggingAppointmentObserver ..|> AppointmentObserver

AppointmentService --> ClinicConfiguration : opening hours
BillingService --> ClinicConfiguration : consultation fee

'============================================================================

note bottom of AbstractBillingStrategy
  calculate() is final. Every pricing rule
  therefore works out its amounts in the
  same order, applies the loyalty discount
  the same way, and rounds money in one
  place. A subclass fills in three steps and
  cannot change the shape of the sum.
end note

note right of SurgicalBillingStrategy
  The three rules genuinely differ, which is
  what makes Strategy honest here rather
  than decorative:

  Standard      treatment + consultation
  Surgical      adds 15% sterilisation first
  Consultation  waives the fee, because
                charging it on top of a
                check-up bills the patient
                twice for one thing
end note

note right of AppointmentService
  The subject does not know who is
  listening. Spring finds every
  AppointmentObserver and hands them over,
  so adding SMS reminders means writing one
  class and changing nothing here.

  announce() calls each observer inside its
  own try. A mail server being down must
  never undo an appointment the patient is
  expecting.
end note

legend bottom
  |= |= Pattern |= Why it fits here |= What it cost |
  | 1 | Factory | one place decides which pricing rule a treatment gets | the categories are hardcoded in a Set; a column on treatments would be better |
  | 2 | Strategy | three genuinely different pricing rules, chosen at run time | the arithmetic is no longer visible when reading BillingService |
  | 3 | Template Method | stops the three rules drifting apart on rounding and loyalty | one more layer of inheritance to follow |
  | 4 | Observer | booking announces itself without knowing who cares | reading register() does not reveal that an email is sent |
  | 5 | Singleton | one set of clinic settings, read constantly, changed rarely | cached values go stale if a manager edits MySQL directly; reload() exists for that |
end legend

@enduml
